This is actually a strong hackathon idea because it solves a real problem that millions of 
middle-class families face. Many families own one or two properties, but all records are 
scattered across paper files, WhatsApp chats, bank statements, and physical folders. Important 
dates like tax payments, rent collection, or agreement renewals are often forgotten. 
Here's a more polished version of the idea. 
Problem Statement 
PropertyPal – A Smart Digital Property Management System for Families 
Many middle-class families purchase plots, flats, agricultural land, or rental properties as 
long-term investments. However, there is no simple platform where they can securely store all 
property-related information in one place. 
As a result: 
● Important legal documents are misplaced. 
● Families forget property tax, maintenance, electricity bills, or rent due dates. 
● Ownership history becomes difficult to trace. 
● Heirs often don't know where documents are stored. 
● Rental income and expenses are not tracked properly. 
● Property appreciation and investment returns are never analyzed. 
The goal is to build a secure digital property locker that helps families manage every aspect of 
their property from purchase to resale. 
Solution 
PropertyVault 
A digital locker and intelligent property manager. 
Instead of using multiple notebooks, folders, and reminders, the app becomes a complete digital 
record for every property. 
